{"id":"n-20261020-kw3afh","category":"sports","display_title":"Cristiano Ronaldo Suspended for Thirty Days","display_title_he":"כריסטיאנו רונאלדו הושעה לשלושים יום","short_summary":"Portuguese football star Cristiano Ronaldo received a 30-day suspension and a small fine after leaving the national team camp in September.","english_level":"C1","words":444,"reading_time":3,"image":null,"sources":[{"name":"Ynet","domain":"ynet.co.il","url":"https://www.ynet.co.il/sport/worldsoccer/article/80hnrmnjq","title":"אחרי הסערה בנבחרת פורטוגל: נחשף עונשו של רונאלדו","published_at":"2026-10-19T17:38:17.000Z"},{"name":"Walla","domain":"sports.walla.co.il","url":"https://sports.walla.co.il/item/3872927","title":"אחרי שנטש את מחנה נבחרת פורטוגל: נחשף עונשו של כריסטיאנו רונאלדו","published_at":"2026-10-19T20:24:00.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-19T17:38:17.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-20T06:22:30.210Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":9,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["The Portuguese Football Federation has officially concluded a disciplinary case involving national team captain Cristiano Ronaldo by handing the veteran forward, who is forty-one years of age, a thirty-day suspension alongside a modest fine of two hundred and fifty-five euros. According to official reports from the disciplinary committee, the sanction follows a deliberate breach of regulations that occurred late last month when the player abruptly abandoned the national team camp in Copenhagen just one day prior to a UEFA Nations League fixture against Denmark. This dramatic departure happened on the thirtieth of September, unfolding against a backdrop of emerging disagreements with national team manager Jorge Jesus.","The entire controversy initially ignited after Ronaldo was left sitting on the bench and did not participate during a match where Portugal secured a two-to-one victory over Norway within the same tournament. Following his sudden departure from the squad, the forward subsequently missed two additional matches, which ended in further victories for Portugal against both Denmark and Norway. Public reaction to the unexpected incident was heavily critical across the country, prompting the star player to issue a formal public apology directed both to his teammates and to the broader public in Portugal, while explicitly affirming that he still considers himself an integral part of the national team setup.","Remarkably, reports indicate that Ronaldo personally urged the federation to apply a strict penalty without any mitigating circumstances, stepping forward to request his own punishment. In statements shared across digital social networks, he openly acknowledged his unique position within the squad, writing that he is not merely an ordinary player but the captain of the group, which serves as an aggravating factor. He emphasized that although he had already apologized, he understood that his actions demanded tangible consequences.","Despite the formal suspension handed down by the disciplinary council under Article 160(1) of the disciplinary regulations, administrative timelines suggest that the penalty will not ultimately prevent Ronaldo from rejoining the international squad for upcoming fixtures. Because the suspension formally traces back to the initial incident at the end of September, his eligibility is expected to be fully restored in time for matches scheduled for mid-November, specifically an encounter against Denmark on the fourteenth of the month followed three days later by a match against Wales in Cardiff. Nevertheless, whether the Al-Nassr striker will actually feature on the pitch under the guidance of Jorge Jesus remains entirely at the discretion of the manager. Their relationship has faced intense scrutiny following the recent rift, and even the player's sister, Elma Aveiro, recently addressed the likelihood of his return by suggesting that the current situation leans more toward a negative outcome than a positive one."],"facts":[{"fact":"Cristiano Ronaldo was suspended for 30 days and fined 255 euros by the Portuguese Football Federation.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"The disciplinary action stems from Ronaldo leaving the national team's training camp in Copenhagen on September 30 before a Nations League match against Denmark.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Ronaldo himself suggested the punishment after apologizing to his teammates and the public in Portugal.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"The 41-year-old player missed matches against Denmark and Norway, but is expected to be eligible to return for November's upcoming fixtures.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Manager Jorge Jesus will need to decide whether to recall the Al-Nassr forward following tensions between the two.","sources":[2]}],"glossary":[{"text":"Portuguese","lemma":"Portuguese","pos":"adjective","he":"פורטוגלי","name":"פורטוגזי"},{"text":"Football","lemma":"Football","pos":"noun","he":"כדורגל","name":"כדורגל"},{"text":"Federation","lemma":"Federation","pos":"noun","he":"התאחדות","name":"התאחדות"},{"text":"has","lemma":"have","pos":"verb","he":"יש / עזר","name":false},{"text":"officially","lemma":"officially","pos":"adverb","he":"רשמית","name":false},{"text":"concluded","lemma":"conclude","pos":"verb","he":"סיים","name":false},{"text":"disciplinary","lemma":"disciplinary","pos":"adjective","he":"משמעתי","name":false},{"text":"case","lemma":"case","pos":"noun","he":"תיק","name":false},{"text":"involving","lemma":"involve","pos":"verb","he":"המעורב ב- / שכולל","name":false},{"text":"national","lemma":"national","pos":"adjective","he":"לאומי","name":false},{"text":"team","lemma":"team","pos":"noun","he":"נבחרת","name":false},{"text":"captain","lemma":"captain","pos":"noun","he":"קפטן","name":false},{"text":"Cristiano","lemma":"Cristiano","pos":"proper noun","he":"כריסטיאנו","name":"כריסטיאנו"},{"text":"Ronaldo","lemma":"Ronaldo","pos":"proper noun","he":"רונאלדו","name":"רונאלדו"},{"text":"by","lemma":"by","pos